# Round XXIX Track C — `Dict.iter().enumerate()` (chained). `DictIter[K,V]`
# is a 2-field iter struct; the pre-fix fast-path read `Field(2)` and
# panicked. Post-fix: the receiver-type gate sees `DictIter` as non-Array
# and falls through to the general iterable protocol; iterating the
# `EnumerateIter[DictIter[String, int], (String, int)]` prints the
# insertion-ordered index-tagged entries.
int main():
    Dict[String, int] d = {"a": 1, "b": 2}
    for (i, kv) in d.iter().enumerate():
        print(f"{i}: {kv._0}={kv._1}")
    return 0
